\f1\fs26 The copter dropped them a mere hundred metres from Elvi Central and then immediately returned to collect Shakti. The pilot, under instructions from Shakti, deleted any record of the flight from the on board data-base. \
In the quarter there was nothing but bars where everyone was welcome - to be fleeced. Your money was wanted here in the quarter and it would not be allowed to leave. The first joint Sarah and Cracker stumbled into was not unlike every other bar in the vicinity \'96 a sleazy dimly lit dive with ridiculously expensive drinks, painted whores at 450mm centres, but excellent entertainment. They were still quite a sight in their full-length white crime scene jump-suits, but compared to some of the patrons they were not out altogether of the ordinary. \
\'93Good evening. I\'92m Elvine and I will be your beverage and food delivery system tonight. Would you like a table or a place at the bar?\'94 Asked the waitress. Elvine was the most the common-name for a female Elvis and she was a quintessential representative of the genome. Her hair was pitch black, perfectly straight and slicked straight back from her forehead in a giant bouffant. Although the nightclub was dimly lit, she was sporting the most outrageously large sunglasses and ridiculous white dress with white leather tassels and rhinestones everywhere. \
\'93Well Elvine, we would like a table tonight, if that is okay?\'94 Cracker said most politely. The Elvi were notoriously sensitive to the ill-mannered, but were saccharine sweet to those who displayed even the most rudimentary etiquette. \
\'93Well ain\'92t you a well-manner young man. Y\'92all just follow little old me and I\'92ll get you the best table in the house.\'94 She turned and snaked her way through the drunken patrons to a tiny, but well positioned booth in direct line of the Elvis show that was presently blasting out a song and dance routine. There were no less than 12 Elvi in flares jumping, dancing and karate kicking their way through tune after tune. The crowd were loving it and so was Sarah. She had never seen or heard anything like it. They called it a Vegas Show and it was very good.\
\'93This looks perfect. Thank you Elvine.\'94 \
\'93You two have a good time. Would you like to start with a beverage?\'94\
\'93Beer?\'94 Cracker looked at Sarah who nodded. \'93Yes, Beer it is. Could you keep them coming, we have had a pretty rough night.\'94\
\'93Keep the suds coming? I sure can honey.\'94 She move closer and whispered in Cracker\'92s ear, \'93I get off in two hours if this one doesn\'92t work out sweetheart\'94 and she disappeared into the crowd. She re-appeared in double quick time, gently placing the bottles of lager on napkins. \'93I\'92ll be back shortly with two more. Are you sure you two can keep up?\'94\
\'93Just keep them coming,\'94 Sarah said and then said quietly to Elvine, \'93I don\'92t think this one is going to work out. When do you get off work?\'94 Elvine\'92s face quickly became flushed and she scuttled off to another table without a word.\
\'93How did you hear what she said over this noise?\'94 Cracker was genuinely intrigued. \
\'93You cannot read lips? I have seen her say that to three men since we got here. She knows how to sell beer.\'94\
\'93Beer sells itself.\'94\
\'93Where is the glass?\'94\
\'93Drink it out of the bottle, L.5.\'94 He said before drawing the bottle to his lips and taking enormous sucks on its slender neck, slurping down the cold, cleansing ale in giant loud gulps. \'93Woo! I really needed that,\'94 he said, gasping for air and slamming the bottle down hard. The remaining contents then billowed up into a thick froth and gushed out, pouring down the neck and forming a white puddle. \
\'93It\'92s a boy!\'94 Sarah giggled. \'93I think you just illustrated all the reasons I prefer to use a glass. Here\'92s to new experiences.\'94 Sarah then drained the bottle in one go, not swallowing, but pouring the contents directly into her gullet and then place the dead marine on the table. \'93A girl has to know how to control her gag reflex.\'94\
\'93One of the tricks you learned in finishing school?\'94 
\f2\i I am definitely in love.
